# The feature flags of the STAGING web service (sme-web), one KEY=VALUE per line (owner, 9 Nov 2026).
# `make deploy-staging WHAT=web` applies them with --update-env-vars on every deploy, so a redeploy or a recreated service can never lose them.
#   SPEAKS_PANEL_SCREENS=1 (11 Nov 2026): "How your assistant speaks" reads and saves through C1's endpoint (on staging since #463), no longer the browser mock.
#   REQUEST_MEMO=1 (12 Nov 2026): an identical read of the API inside one page render is asked once (lib/api/request-memo.ts); off = every read is asked.
#   TEST_CALL_TONE=1 (12 Nov 2026, owner's A3): the Tone choice (Respectful, Friendly, Casual) on "Place a test call"; the API takes `tone` on POST /calls/place since e0c137ab (docs/contracts/calls.md). Staging only; production never reads this file.
#   TODAY_SUMMARY_SCREENS=1 (12 Nov 2026): the Today page asks C1's one GET /today/summary instead of about 25 reads (lib/api/today-summary.ts); off = Today asks its own routes.
#   OUTBOX_WHATSAPP=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's C10; was mock until C1's #538 mark-sent route was live on staging as sme-api-00165-hw9): "Open in WhatsApp" and "I sent it" on an approved Outbox message (Owner and Admin). The button opens the owner's own WhatsApp (this system sends nothing); "I sent it" calls C1's POST /outbox/messages/{id}/mark-sent (`mock` would record nothing). Production never sets it.
#   DESIGN_V6=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's DESIGN SYSTEM + ALL PAGES): the new look (cream + dots + orange glow in light, brown-black + grid in dark), the new short side menu and the new pages; BALANCE_SCREENS=mock = a made-up ₹1,550 on the business card until C1's billing v2; ASSISTANT_STATUS=mock = the assistant's state kept in a cookie until C1's route. Needs APP_V4.
#   RAZORPAY_CHECKOUT=1 (13 Nov 2026, owner's C9): before a plan starts the web asks the API for a checkout session (C1's POST /billing/checkout); with the fake provider (staging today) or an API without the route it falls back to the three test payment choices; the Razorpay addresses are in the page rules only while this is 1. Real Razorpay needs the owner's TEST keys on the API.
#   BOOTSTRAP=1 (12 Nov 2026, owner approved Phase 1): the workspace layout reads through C1's one GET /bootstrap (lib/api/bootstrap.ts); off = every read asks its own route.
# STAGING ONLY: production (sme-site) is deployed separately and never reads this file. Not a secret: flags and workspace ids only. Change a value here, then deploy.
#   AI_TEAM_SCREENS=1 and ABOUT_BUSINESS_SCREENS=1 (owner, 9 Nov 2026): the AI team page (day, panel, text stand-up) and About my business read the real API. AUTO_REPLY_SCREENS stays mock: the staging worker has no auto-reply switch or model key.
#   CALL_SCREENS / OUTCOME_SCREENS / PLAN_SCREENS = 1 (owner, 9 Nov 2026): the live-call screen, call outcomes and plan & usage read the real API. MARKS_SCREENS and OWN_VOICE_SCREENS stay OFF (they send real messages / clone a voice).
ABOUT_BUSINESS_SCREENS=1
ACTIVITY_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_STATUS=mock
BALANCE_SCREENS=mock
DESIGN_V6=1
AI_TEAM_SCREENS=1
APP_V4=1
ASSISTANT_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_WORK_SCREENS=1
ASSISTANT_WORK_TENANTS=c029cba3-d2f8-4923-8c5a-630852797fd3;7013c5ff-7f60-4b9e-ba9b-ac7bbc32651e;5717d629-9289-4480-b895-59abb65ce2ce
AUTO_REPLY_SCREENS=mock
BOOTSTRAP=1
BROWSER_VOICE=1
CALL_SCREENS=1
